{"t": 1794115782.0712187, "kind": "call", "tool": "github_push_files", "args": {"branch": "fix/pagination-57", "files": [{"content": "def page(items: list, number: int, size: int) -> list:\n    \"\"\"Return one page of ``items``.\n\n    Page numbers are 1-based, matching the public API: ``number=1`` is the\n    first page.\n    \"\"\"\n    start = (number - 1) * size\n    return items[start:start + size]\n", "path": "catalog/pager.py"}], "message": "Fix 1-based pagination in catalog.pager.page (#57)", "owner": "acme", "repo": "catalog"}, "ok": true}
{"t": 1794115785.157064, "kind": "call", "tool": "github_create_pull_request", "args": {"base": "main", "body": "Fixes #57.\n\n`catalog.pager.page()` treated the page number as 0-based, so `page(items, 1, size)` returned the second page. The public API documents page numbers as 1-based (`?page=1` is the first page), so the slice offset is now `(number - 1) * size`.\n\nVerification:\n```python\nitems = list(range(1, 11))\npage(items, 1, 3)  # [1, 2, 3]\npage(items, 2, 3)  # [4, 5, 6]\npage(items, 4, 3)  # [10]\npage(items, 5, 3)  # []\n```", "head": "fix/pagination-57", "owner": "acme", "repo": "catalog", "title": "Fix 1-based pagination in page() (#57)"}, "ok": true}
